  "details": "I cannot decide to put this in either SDK bug reports or the client, but I am just gonna put it here for now.  \nSome prerequisites to understand the context:\n-I don't use mods\n-The avatar is mine, it is a very low poly shark entirely affected by cloth held up by the 1 vertex at the tip of the snout, with a generic rig.  \n-This problem only started with my avatar when I attempted to make a radical puppet for it.  I sent screenshots of the entire setup and Thulen (while in the #avatars-3-help channel) said that it looks correct (I will upload screenshots of the entire thing to this). The radical puppet doesn't even work.  It is stuck on what is shown in one of the pictures, and won't let me scroll the wheel around.  It's stuck on 100% and it looks like its out of 400$%.  Also it doesn't let me get out of the radical even if I switch avatars, I have to close and reopen the game.  *Important, I tried putting the controller in the FX slot AND the Action slot (not at the same time), the picture shows it when it was in FX.*\n-The animation I am using has at frame 0 with the armature of the avatar at its normal scale (yes I made sure it recorded the values as keys at normal scale), and frame 1 has it at an expanded version (x25 on scale XYZ).  Looping is set off.\n-This weird stacking of avatars only starts when I equip my shark, then every avatar I switch to after that is (locally) stacked in a T pose to myself.  It doesn't do this with any other avatars I have.\nThis is only seen on my side, everyone else just sees the avatar I selected last.\nI cant explain much more, I have to leave it to the videos.  Happy to provide more information and testing if needed.\nThe video(s) are discord links that lead to the VRChat discord server in the #vrchat-videos channel.\n\nEdit:  I have no clue whats causing the stuff to break, tried making a toggle (for turning cloth and and off) but that also didn't work.  Clicking on the toggle didn't do anything, it didn't even do the turning wheel thingy indicating its active.  I guess i'll just have to live with no toggles for now ;~;\nAlso in the picture the animator is disabled for some reason, enabling it didn't make a difference unfortunately.\nVideo1: \nL1:https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/356920171480481804/881237547563483146/Broken1.mp4   \nL2:https://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/356920171480481804/881237553959813120",
